<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!-- Checks the economy's game-free parts outside the game: the credit rating's arithmetic, the lending terms and the
       phone's fee, the credit file's cap and folding, its line in the save across versions, how the game's loans
       are told apart, and (Checks2.cs) the credit products, what happens when payments are missed, consolidation,
       the lender of last resort and the ways out of debt, and (Checks3.cs) the city's economy: twenty years of the model
       from many seeds, the central bank's rule, the adjustments, the rate the credit side reads and the save's line,
       and (Checks5.cs) running a business: staff, insurance, marketing, tax and the accountant, cash off the books,
       licences and its line in the save, and (RotaChecks.cs) the staff rota planner: the rota itself, the hours worth
       opening and the people a week takes, and (TableChecks.cs) the table model every app's table is ordered,
       filtered and summed by, and the categories of the cash flow, and (OnlineChecks.cs) the online shops: demand,
       orders, picking, rounds, lateness and the rating, returns, the day's book, the bound on what a site adds and
       its line in the save, and (ServicesChecks.cs) the cleaning service and selling a business: the round,
       what a visit does, contracts, a business's value, the market and the money on the day, and (BrandChecks.cs) brands and franchises: recognition, standards, a
       franchised shop's day, every way an agreement ends, a shop under a city chain and the save's line, and (ManagerChecks.cs) the managers of the player's places: each kind of decision inside its limit, mistakes bounded, the stock arithmetic, who decides, the company asking again when they are off, overrides, undo windows and the save's line, and (KeptPriceChecks.cs) prices kept for a chain or a brand: always
       inside the chain's range, the district's adjustment bounded, a price changed by something else put back, and (EstateChecks.cs) property:
       the market, a purchase on the existing mortgage, tenancies, works, a sale, the agency, a hotel's night, car hire,
       the yearly returns and the save's line, a building sold and put back as the player's for nothing handed back to its buyer (SoldBackChecks.cs), and (MarketChecks.cs) the city's stock market: prices over thousands of days,
       trading and what it costs, orders, dividends, splits, failures, candles, the analysis tools, the tape and the save's line, and
       (LedgerChecks.cs) the City Ledger: what each piece is, its headline, the subscription's round, the copy, the page's choices and the save's line, and
       (NewsstandChecks.cs) the City Ledger online: the titles' prices, the connection rule, the weeks, the pass, the editions kept, what each title prints and the save's line, and
       (SharedCityChecks.cs) the shared city of a Going Public session: its messages, another version's, a damaged one, and each shared part applied to a guest's own state, and (FlareChecks.cs) Flare, the social media app, and (EmpireChecks.cs) the
       books of a dealership of Empire Motors, another author's mod: its takings and costs, a share of what has no address,
       its stock among its records and what the tax deducts, and (FameChecks.cs) Standing:
       wealth, recognition, the four reputations, the daily round, the street, the press, the city's requests and the save's line, and
       (PermadeathChecks.cs) Permadeath: the odds, the warnings first, when nothing can happen, the flu's course, the switch per save, a dead save, the life's line and the obituary's sentences, and
       (DistrictChecks.cs) the district view on the city map: the layers' scales, the bands, the key's ranges, the colours, the crime log and its line in the save, and
       (InteriorChecks.cs) interiors and decor: the decor score's diminishing returns, caps and variety, the target by floor area, wear, dirt, a refresh, the district's
       standard, every effect's size and cap, the parts that step aside for the other authors' two mods, the save's line and the other features' rules that take its part, and
       (BusInsideChecks.cs) the bus ride seen: the places the clips want on the bus, every path clear of the seats, the way off, the pull-away and the fare given back, and
       (OwnBankChecks.cs) the player's own bank: the rival banks' rates, the city's savers and borrowers, defaults, arrears, the regulator's ratio, a run, the fund, a sale and the save's line, and (DealerChecks.cs) the car dealership: a car's worth, the lot, the market,
       haggling and the trade auction, customers and their offers, the dealership's finance and warranties, the books and the save's line, and a month of a reference dealership, and
       (ShowroomFloorChecks.cs) the Car Showroom's floor: the visitors an hour shows, the bays and their save line, the camera's limits and the texts, and
       (CartQueueChecks.cs) the pavement drinks cart's queue: a customer who cannot get to the cart, or is no longer its own, leaves the queue at once, is no walk-off and is replaced, and (CartSoundChecks.cs) the drinks cart heard: the order cue, its one reminder and the till by their rules, the gig calling them where the order starts, waits and is paid, the option and the texts, and
       (TaxiComfortChecks.cs) ride fares' easier passengers: the two tables, a rough ride under each and the gig reading only the table, and (RivalFirstChecks.cs) when the first rival tycoon comes forward by the option, and
       (RivalChecks.cs, RivalReviewChecks.cs) the rival tycoons: their holdings, growth by the player's thresholds, the pace of their moves, each move's bounds, the counters and a takeover, the same moves from a seed, the save's line and the texts, and
       (UiChecks.cs) the interface kit: its tokens, fonts, text, motion, focus, every registered screen at every frame in every language and both looks, its sources and texts, and (SessionChecks.cs) the desk sessions: the registry, the schedule, the furniture, managers' seeded choices, the save's line and the weekly team meeting through the people part's rules, and (TechScaleChecks.cs) the tech sector's money scale: budgets, the audience to sales relation and its bands, a studio over ten years against the end game, and the one month rule for monthly bills, and (EndScaleChecks.cs) the end game at scale: each late venture's costs, upkeep, crews and income by size, its payback, an old save phased in, the option off and its texts, and (OfficeChecks.cs) running for office: who may stand and when, the law on donors, the vote model by district, the campaign's doings, the council's odds, the city's budget, approval, recall and the save's lines, and (PhotoChecks.cs) the Camera and the Gallery: a photo's name and folder, the cap,
       deleted saves, the order from a folder, the photo and its small copy handed to Flare, the camera's rules and the restore of what it borrows, and (GalleryChecks.cs)
       the Gallery: why a photo would not open, one tap to see it whole, the albums, the days and their order, the rows built in view, the photo before
       and after, the favourites kept beside the photos and the texts
       Compiles the mod's own files, so it checks exactly what ships.
       the lender of last resort and the ways out of debt, and (VenturesChecks.cs) investors, the pitch, deals and the
       stock market. Compiles the mod's own files, so it checks exactly what ships.
       Run: dotnet run -c Release (from this folder). Exit code 0 = all checks passed. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <RootNamespace>RealLifeOverhaul</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

